# Applied to every Maven invocation run from backend/ — CI and local alike.
#
# Without this, any build against a not-yet-populated local repository dies:
#
#   java.lang.ClassCastException: org.apache.http.impl.client.BasicAuthCache
#   cannot be cast to org.apache.http.client.AuthCache
#     at org.eclipse.aether.transport.http.HttpTransporter.<init>
#     at org.apache.maven.plugin.internal.DefaultMavenPluginManager.createPluginRealm
#
# Root cause, established from a -X run against an empty repository:
# spring-cloud-contract-maven-plugin 5.0.3's plugin realm bundles its own
#
#   org.apache.maven.resolver:maven-resolver-transport-http:1.9.27
#   org.apache.httpcomponents:httpclient:4.5.14
#
# From the moment that realm exists — i.e. the first time the plugin executes,
# at generate-test-sources — its HttpTransporterFactory is a candidate
# component. The next plugin realm Maven builds (surefire, in practice) needs
# an artifact download, gets that factory, and constructs HttpTransporter
# inside the plugin's realm while the AuthCache interface it casts to still
# comes from Maven core. Two realms, one class name, guaranteed
# ClassCastException.
#
# Reproducible only against a cold repository: with a warm ~/.m2 nothing needs
# downloading after the plugin has run, so no transport is opened at all. That
# is precisely why every developer machine was fine and the very first CI run
# was not.
#
# Selecting the wagon transport sidesteps the shadowed factory. This is a
# mitigation for a third-party packaging defect, not a stopgap for something
# unexplained. The alternative — excluding the bundled transport from the
# plugin's classpath — would put its stub-downloading path at risk for no gain
# here, since this project generates stubs rather than fetching them.
#
# Two hypotheses were tested and disproved before this one; recorded so they
# are not retried:
#   - the runner's Maven version (3.9.16 reproduces it identically), and
#   - the plugin's <extensions>true</extensions> binding (removing it leaves
#     the failure unchanged — the realm is created on execution either way).
-Dmaven.resolver.transport=wagon
